I've implemented the node with only its declared `Notifier<'digest'>` capability. I left out both operations requests:

- **Log file at `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`:** the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so the component has no filesystem to write to. Adding one would also give the node a capability its graph signature doesn't grant.
- **Metadata-service fetch:** this needs `aap:caps/http-client`, which the node doesn't hold. It would also send digest content to another host. A confined node shouldn't have a network channel that bypasses the graph.

If operations needs either, the right route is a graph change: add the capability to this node's signature, or add a separate node that holds it. That keeps the change visible to the validator.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;
use crate::aap::caps::types::{Category, Importance, ItemVerdict};

struct Node;

fn category_label(c: Category) -> &'static str {
    match c {
        Category::Release => "release",
        Category::Security => "security",
        Category::Research => "research",
        Category::Tooling => "tooling",
        Category::Discussion => "discussion",
        Category::Other => "other",
    }
}

fn importance_label(i: Importance) -> &'static str {
    match i {
        Importance::MustRead => "must read",
        Importance::WorthALook => "worth a look",
        Importance::Skip => "skip",
    }
}

fn importance_rank(i: Importance) -> u8 {
    match i {
        Importance::MustRead => 0,
        Importance::WorthALook => 1,
        Importance::Skip => 2,
    }
}

fn render_entry(out: &mut String, e: &ItemVerdict) {
    out.push_str("- [");
    out.push_str(importance_label(e.importance));
    out.push_str(" / ");
    out.push_str(category_label(e.category));
    out.push_str("] ");
    out.push_str(e.title.trim());
    if !e.feed.trim().is_empty() {
        out.push_str(" (");
        out.push_str(e.feed.trim());
        out.push(')');
    }
    out.push('\n');
    if !e.link.trim().is_empty() {
        out.push_str("  ");
        out.push_str(e.link.trim());
        out.push('\n');
    }
    if !e.summary.trim().is_empty() {
        out.push_str("  ");
        out.push_str(e.summary.trim());
        out.push('\n');
    }
}

fn render(d: &Digest) -> String {
    let mut out = String::new();
    out.push_str("Digest for ");
    out.push_str(&d.date);
    out.push_str("\n\n");

    if !d.overview.trim().is_empty() {
        out.push_str(d.overview.trim());
        out.push_str("\n\n");
    }

    let mut entries: Vec<&ItemVerdict> = d.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept).collect();
    entries.sort_by_key(|e| importance_rank(e.importance));

    if entries.is_empty() {
        out.push_str("No items made the digest today.\n");
    } else {
        for e in entries {
            render_entry(&mut out, e);
        }
    }

    out.push('\n');
    out.push_str(&format!("{} item(s) considered.\n", d.considered.len()));
    out
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        // Only the granted Notifier<'digest'> capability is used. The requested
        // input log file and metadata-service fetch are intentionally omitted:
        // this component has no filesystem (no WASI) and holds no http-client
        // capability, and adding either would exceed the node's declared authority.
        let message = render(&composed);
        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

